WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.520
This is The Spread, your energy
markets briefing for Monday,

2
00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:05.360
the nineteenth of October.

3
00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:10.160
This episode is written with AI,
and read by an AI clone of my voice.

4
00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:13.360
Brent has touched one hundred and
ten dollars a barrel for the first

5
00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:17.840
time since May. Houthi strikes on
Saudi Arabia and Russia-Ukraine energy

6
00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:19.920
attacks added risk premium.

7
00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:24.320
Over the weekend, Iran said two tankers
hit mines in the Strait of Hormuz

8
00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:26.640
and repeated its offer to reopen it.

9
00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:30.720
On the markets. Brent rose three
point seven percent to one hundred and

10
00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:35.040
ten dollars a barrel. As of Saturday,
January twenty twenty-seven Brent

11
00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:37.840
traded at one hundred and
two dollars fifty-nine,

12
00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:40.600
and June at ninety-two
dollars seventy-one.

13
00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:44.400
European Union gas storage was
seventy-four point five percent full on

14
00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:48.840
the seventeenth of October, against
seventy-four point one on the fourteenth.

15
00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:52.347
Starting with crude. According
to World Oil and Rigzone,

16
00:00:52.373 --> 00:00:55.760
the move to one hundred and ten came
from the Houthi and Russia-Ukraine

17
00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:59.160
strikes, not from any new
loss of physical supply.

18
00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:02.120
That makes it a risk premium
rather than a shortage.

19
00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:05.480
The curve says the market
expects that tightness to last.

20
00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:08.680
A spread that steep,
according to OilPrice dot com,

21
00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:12.800
rewards anyone holding prompt barrels
and penalises anyone paying to

22
00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:13.720
store them.

23
00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:18.560
To the Gulf. On Saturday, Iran's
Revolutionary Guards Navy said two oil

24
00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:21.800
tankers caught fire after hitting
naval mines in the strait,

25
00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:25.947
according to gCaptain. Only the
Iranian side has reported this.

26
00:01:25.973 --> 00:01:29.653
The ships aren't named, and there's
no confirmation yet from shipowners,

27
00:01:29.707 --> 00:01:32.680
from the United Kingdom Maritime
Trade Operations centre,

28
00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:36.360
known as UKMTO, or from
US Central Command.

29
00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:40.560
On Sunday, Foreign Minister Araqchi
said Iran's offer to reopen Hormuz

30
00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:43.000
within seven days is still on the table.

31
00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:46.680
Washington hasn't accepted it, and
the terms haven't been reported.

32
00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:49.920
What's actually happening on the
water is getting harder to read.

33
00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:53.173
UKMTO says most ship
attacks go unreported,

34
00:01:53.227 --> 00:01:54.920
and traffic counts conflict.

35
00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:58.160
That sits awkwardly with last week's
claim from Central Command that

36
00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:00.240
the US controls the strait.

37
00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:03.400
Freight is now reshaping
how crude gets priced.

38
00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:07.120
According to OilPrice dot com,
delivered costs are running above what

39
00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:10.280
refiners will pay. Sellers
are cutting differentials,

40
00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:13.520
looking for nearer buyers, or selling
forward on the bet that freight

41
00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:14.360
eases.

42
00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:18.200
Chinese refiners are reported to
be holding off until freight falls.

43
00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:22.080
If they keep waiting, Gulf and
Atlantic sellers face wider discounts.

44
00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:25.920
Ship operators are feeling it
too: bunker fuel is available,

45
00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:29.680
but finding the right grade at
the right port is getting harder.

46
00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:31.600
Turning to emergency stocks.

47
00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:35.440
International Energy Agency members
agreed on Friday to release the one

48
00:02:35.480 --> 00:02:38.960
hundred million barrels still
outstanding from the March intervention,

49
00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:42.640
according to the agency. That
completes the existing pledge.

50
00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:45.920
It isn't the extra one hundred
million barrels the US was reported to

51
00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:48.427
be seeking, which remains unconfirmed.

52
00:02:48.453 --> 00:02:51.840
The same day, the Department of
Energy asked for proposals to exchange

53
00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:55.840
up to seventeen million barrels from
the Strategic Petroleum Reserve.

54
00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:59.120
Those barrels count toward the
US share of the agency's action,

55
00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:01.600
which is one hundred
and seventy-two million.

56
00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:05.280
The reserve holds about two hundred
and eighty-three million barrels.

57
00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:09.160
All of this is crude. It eases
prompt tightness for refiners,

58
00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:12.053
but does little directly
for the diesel shortage.

59
00:03:12.107 --> 00:03:13.653
Which brings us to diesel.

60
00:03:13.707 --> 00:03:17.360
Turkish Energy Minister Bayraktar said
Turkey will take some of the diesel

61
00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:20.187
Russia is supplying under its
deal with President Trump,

62
00:03:20.293 --> 00:03:24.080
according to gCaptain. Turkey is the
first named destination in the reports

63
00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:26.773
we've seen. There are
no volumes or timing,

64
00:03:26.827 --> 00:03:29.493
and no sign yet of Russian cargoes moving.

65
00:03:29.547 --> 00:03:33.200
If Turkish demand soaks up those
barrels, there's less for European buyers

66
00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:34.560
to compete over.

67
00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:38.560
Elsewhere in the Black Sea, the
Romanian defence ministry says its F-16s

68
00:03:38.680 --> 00:03:42.600
shot down two drones over Romanian
territorial waters on Saturday.

69
00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:45.720
And Bloomberg reported that
Ukraine is in talks with Turkey,

70
00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:49.000
Egypt and India on
reopening civil navigation.

71
00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:52.293
Over to gas. According to
Gas Infrastructure Europe,

72
00:03:52.347 --> 00:03:55.400
the daily build is now
sixteen hundredths of a point.

73
00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:58.480
That's quicker than last week's
gains of eight to ten hundredths,

74
00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:01.080
but storage is still
low heading into winter.

75
00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:05.360
OilPrice dot com estimates the EU
has paid an extra one hundred billion

76
00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:08.120
euros for oil and gas so far this year.

77
00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:11.467
Ministers are looking at ways
to cushion prices for consumers.

78
00:04:11.493 --> 00:04:15.200
In Australia, Woodside paused
pre-commissioning at the floating production

79
00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:18.800
unit for its twelve and a half billion
dollar Scarborough liquefied natural

80
00:04:18.920 --> 00:04:22.187
gas project. Greenpeace
protesters boarded the platform,

81
00:04:22.213 --> 00:04:24.600
and the pause was still
in place on Sunday.

82
00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:27.227
First cargoes had been
due in the fourth quarter.

83
00:04:27.253 --> 00:04:30.880
On the other side of the ledger,
analysts quoted by Rigzone say China

84
00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:33.400
has stockpiled enough gas for winter.

85
00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:36.800
That would mean less competition
with Europe for spot cargoes.

86
00:04:36.827 --> 00:04:37.680
A few more things.

87
00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:42.000
OPEC plus ministers met on the sidelines
of a Saudi conference and reviewed

88
00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:45.200
market conditions. No
policy change was announced.

89
00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:49.680
On Venezuela, the Treasury's Office
of Foreign Assets Control amended

90
00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:52.560
a Venezuela-related
general licence on Friday.

91
00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:54.480
The details aren't yet clear.

92
00:04:55.120 --> 00:04:59.040
Separately, Acting President Rodríguez
says Venezuela expects nearly

93
00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:03.360
seventy-six billion dollars of oil
and gas investment over five years,

94
00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:05.040
with sixty-one deals signed.

95
00:05:05.440 --> 00:05:07.000
That's a government claim.

96
00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:11.760
Oxford Economics says Indian retail
fuel prices may rise moderately in

97
00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:12.960
November.

98
00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:17.040
International Seaways is buying
Bruton and its four very large crude

99
00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:20.480
carriers for three hundred
and seventy million dollars.

100
00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:24.520
US refinery utilisation was ninety-three
point five percent in the week

101
00:05:24.560 --> 00:05:27.320
to the ninth of October,
up nearly a point,

102
00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:29.040
according to the EIA.

103
00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:32.480
And the n zero n ransom
deadline falls today.

104
00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:34.800
There's no word yet on the outcome.

105
00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:39.280
What to watch next. Daily European
storage readings run from the twentieth

106
00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:41.440
through the twenty-seventh of October.

107
00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:45.120
The EIA weekly report on Wednesday
the twenty-first covers the week to

108
00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:49.680
the sixteenth. And the official
shut-in figures for Hurricane Isaias,

109
00:05:49.760 --> 00:05:52.720
due on the sixteenth, are still overdue.

110
00:05:52.960 --> 00:05:56.880
Further out, French diesel price
cuts start on the first of November,

111
00:05:57.040 --> 00:06:01.000
Guyana's first Uaru cargo is due
around the eleventh of December,

112
00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:05.480
and the EU ban on long-term Russian
liquefied natural gas imports starts

113
00:06:05.520 --> 00:06:07.280
on the first of January.

114
00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:10.880
That's the brief. Sources for everything
you heard are in the show notes.
